Phil Taylor wrote:

> ...  a most important desideratum: that
> of placing a float so that it is visible from its point of reference,
> \stress {even if that means placing the figure on the page _preceding_
> the point of reference}.

I must admit to puzzlement about when such a placement (figure on a
preceding, facing page) would actually occur. Can you give some
examples?  If a figure reference occurs 5cm from the bottom of page 59
(right-hand page) and the figure is 6cm tall, I don't see how moving
the figure to page 58 will help anything: it will most likely push the
figure reference to page 60, leaving the figure once again not visible
from the point of reference.

